  "templated": [
    {
      "template": "ach_transfer.${verb}",
      "source": "supabase/functions/api/ach.ts:488",
      "expands_to": [
        "ach_transfer.settled",
        "ach_transfer.returned"
      ],
      "note": "verb is 'settled' | 'returned'; only emitted where money MOVED, so a pre-settlement return emits nothing"
    },
    {
      "template": "entity.${to}",
      "source": "supabase/functions/api/entities.ts",
      "expands_to": [
        "entity.active",
        "entity.disabled",
        "entity.archived"
      ],
      "note": "targets of the entity state machine (pending is the initial state, never a transition TARGET, so entity.pending is never emitted)"
    },
    {
      "template": "account.${to}",
      "source": "supabase/functions/api/accounts.ts",
      "expands_to": [
        "account.frozen",
        "account.closed",
        "account.open"
      ],
      "note": "ACCOUNT_TRANSITIONS targets: open<->frozen, both -> closed"
    },
    {
      "template": "account_number.${to}",
      "source": "supabase/functions/api/numbers.ts:191",
      "expands_to": [
        "account_number.active",
        "account_number.disabled",
        "account_number.canceled"
      ]
    },
    {
      "template": "verification.${status}",
      "source": "supabase/functions/api/kyc.ts:158",
      "expands_to": [
        "verification.approved",
        "verification.denied"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "_deliberately_excluded": {
    "what": "The 83 time-based trigger codes the governance calendar can fire.",
    "why": [
      "postCalendarSweep emits String(row.trigger_code) \u2014 whatever code a REGISTERED",
      "obligation carries. So the core can technically emit audit.cycle_timer,",
      "training.annual_cycle.opened, vendor.annual.review.due_at and 80 others.",
      "",
      "Listing them here would move dozens of controls to 'reachable' on the",
      "strength of a CAPABILITY nobody has exercised. Reachability is meant to",
      "answer 'can the core fire this control's trigger', and the honest answer",
      "for an unregistered obligation is no \u2014 the machinery exists, the",
      "obligation does not.",
      "",
      "This is the single largest opportunity in the repo to inflate the coverage",
      "numbers with one JSON edit, which is exactly why it is refused. If these",
      "are ever added it must be driven by what is actually REGISTERED on a real",
      "instance, not by what the code is capable of. See BLUEPRINT 5a."
    ],
    "codes_available_if_registered": 83
  }
}